Z||000003||stimpy||04-15-2000||09:52 AM||||Good point Monkey, what is the original spoiler? If it is an 84 SE, if it has a "wing" on it, then it isn't factory. Correct me if I am wrong, but only 84 w/ a wing is the Indy. And If you have an Indy wing that you are taking off, why replace w/ a GT wing, the only difference being a slightly different angle?  Grizco, we need details! ||||reg||1
Z||000004||grizco||04-15-2000||02:37 PM||||The wing on my car is one of those aluminum ones that appears to be connected to the luggage rack. Will the GT wing bolt on using the original mounting holes or will it leave holes in the decklid that have to be filled later? <BR>Here is the address for the spoiler that I'm looking at. <A HREF="http://store.yahoo.com/gofast/8488ponfierg.html" TARGET=_blank>http://store.yahoo.com/gofast/8488ponfierg.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||stimpy||04-15-2000||02:57 PM||||Then the answer is indeed no, (or is it yes?) Anyhow, the bolt holes for the luggage rack are not the same as the big-ass wing. (not tryin to say anything about wings, just not my personal preference.) I have the luggage rack on my 86 GT and would like to remove it but don't want to mess with filling all the little holes.  Anyone want a rare option on the 86 GT and has a plain gold decklid they want to trade?||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||04-15-2000||03:18 PM||||The answer is no. You'll want to replace the deck lid with a blank one and install the new wing on it. ||||reg||1
